==English==

===Etymology===
Clipping of {{m|en|grotesque}} {{suffix|en||y}}. Compare American {{m|en|grody}}, of same origin. Possibly influenced by {{der|en|gd|grod||rotten, putrid}}, compare {{m+|enm|groti||muddy, slimy}}<!--though etymonline considers the similarity merely superficial/incidental-->.

Originated or popularised by the 1964 film ''[[w:A Hard Day's Night (film)|A Hard Day's Night]]'', starring [[w:The Beatles|the Beatles]] and written by [[w:Alun Owen|Alun Owen]].

